# Manual smoke test for role edit/delete.
# Requires the backend on http://localhost:3001 and an admin token.
# Variables (REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client):
#   @host = http://localhost:3001
#   @token = <admin jwt>
#   @staffRoleId = <id returned by the create request>

@host = http://localhost:3001
@token = replace-me
@staffRoleId = replace-me

### Create a non-system Staff role
POST {{host}}/api/roles
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Staff",
  "description": "Regular staff member with basic permissions"
}

### Update the Staff role
PUT {{host}}/api/roles/{{staffRoleId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Staff Updated",
  "description": "Updated staff role with modified permissions"
}

### Assign permissions to the Staff role
PUT {{host}}/api/roles/{{staffRoleId}}/permissions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "permissionIds": []
}

### Delete the Staff role
DELETE {{host}}/api/roles/{{staffRoleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected behavior
# - The created Staff role has isSystem = false and is editable.
# - It is deletable while no user is assigned to it.
# - Admin, Manager, and Cashier remain system roles and stay locked.
